{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die","id":104955,"title":"Ascension for Exigents: Where gods go to die","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-03T11:08:43-07:00","id":104955,"title":"Ascension for Exigents: Where gods go to die","content":"An Exigent's power comes from and is of the nature of his patron. But what happens if that patron can't do his job anymore? Or even worse: Was slain. There are multiple options what could happen, some of which I'd really love to discuss:<br /> A) A new god takes over that purview and also takes over as the Exigent's patron.<br /> B) &quot;The old gods and the new&quot; The Exigent is basically rebelling against his new boss because he does not see eye to eye. This could turn into a holy war even if both parties involve the Cults and devotees to that purview, effectively turning a small part of the Celestial Bureaucracy into a civil war.<br /> C) The Exigent decides he does not need another as his patron and takes over that part of the Celestial Bureaucracy, as the new God of XYZ.<br /> <br /> (of course those are only 3 of many many scenarios)<br /> <br /> While I like both A and B, C has maybe the greatest potential as a story hook. A human taking over for a god? Scandalous! Perfect hook for a political thriller in Yu-Shan.<br /> <br /> What do you think of those scenarios? Do you have others you'd like to see played out in the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T11:15:20-07:00","id":104962,"title":"","content":"It's not very useful to think of exigence as patronage. Just like the Incarna put their faith on their chosen, so do the gods and their exigents. Power that once given cannot be taken away.<br /> <br /> So patron died? Lots of things will happen, but changes in your powers is not really one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T11:19:16-07:00","id":104965,"title":"","content":"Given that many if not most gods will die in order to obtain the power of the Exigence in the first place, I doubt it really matters all that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T11:21:40-07:00","id":104968,"title":"","content":"Something I've been curious about is if Exigents are always stronger than their patron god. I guess they are other way what's the main benefit of getting an Exigent? Somebody please enlighten me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T11:24:39-07:00","id":104970,"title":"","content":"Okay, maybe I forgot the multitude of possible Exigents. I was talking about Exigents who are at least sympathetic of their &quot;donor&quot; (better word than patron i think) or even of their donor's purview.<br /> <br /> The big problem I have so far: I have no idea where Exigents will be placed in the Celestial Bureaucracy. Or how they will interact with it. But I'm sure it's going to be large part in most more political games, because Yu Shan is Yu Shan. Everything's politics there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T11:27:21-07:00","id":104971,"title":"","content":"I was of the impression that gods often die in the process of creating an Exigent. You're not so much working for a given god as you are the recipient of powers derived from theirs. If they're your boss, it's only in the sense that all but the most desperate of gods would pick an Exigent who is inclined to agree with whatever goals led to creating an Exigent in the first place. This also provides an incentive for not all gods to treat all humans like crap, since if you need an Exigent you probably want it to be someone who likes you.<br /> <br /> Now, if the god of your town's wheat field dies Exalting you and Yu-Shan brings in a replacement, that town has to renegotiate its position with the new god. The presence of the Exigent can do a lot to affect how this negotiation resolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T11:27:25-07:00","id":104972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=104968#post104968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've been curious about is if Exigents are always stronger than their patron god. I guess they are other way what's the main benefit of getting an Exigent? Somebody please enlighten me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably not going to be true, either. Who knows with these dudes ._.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T12:32:36-07:00","id":105019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=104968#post104968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've been curious about is if Exigents are always stronger than their patron god. I guess they are other way what's the main benefit of getting an Exigent? Somebody please enlighten me.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way I've been thinking about it (though as Synapse says, we don't yet know for sure) is that power isn't the only consideration in play. Mortals have their own capabilities before becoming Exalted, and all Exalted still use those capabilities, channeled through the lens of their patron's power.* By contrast, a god's powers necessarily revolve around managing and maintaining their domain, but aren't necessarily going to extend beyond that.<br /> <br /> Look at Ten Sheaves and Janest. The god didn't strike me as especially martially inclined (though I could be wrong; he did have the scythe, unless that was a bonus with Exigence), but his Chosen had trained to help defend the town her entire life. Once Exalted, she could channel his power in that more martial direction, enough to have a shot at fighting off the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> Through Exigence, a god gives up a portion (or sometimes all of) her power and being, and in doing so empowers a mortal who has the will and capabilities to do what is needed with that power. Remember that the word &quot;exigent&quot; means &quot;pressing; demanding.&quot; Going by that and the Janest fiction, the intent (or most common circumstance) is an emergency situation. Potential tagline: &quot;Exigence is for those times when even a god needs a miracle.&quot;<br /> <br /> * Even absent an Ability-/Attribute-based Charmset, 2e Infernals still used their natural Abilities and Attributes (and other traits) in using their powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T12:37:15-07:00","id":105022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=104971#post104971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was of the impression that gods often die in the process of creating an Exigent. You're not so much working for a given god as you are the recipient of powers derived from theirs. If they're your boss, it's only in the sense that all but the most desperate of gods would pick an Exigent who is inclined to agree with whatever goals led to creating an Exigent in the first place. This also provides an incentive for not all gods to treat all humans like crap, since if you need an Exigent you probably want it to be someone who likes you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get the impression that Exigence has that much of an impact on divine/mortal relations. It strikes me as a pretty rare thing: Something you find because there is nothing you can do except throw yourself at the Sun's feet and beg for aid, not something you always keep in your back pocket as a final contingency. Now, the Black Market stuff is obviously different, but I figure those are at least as rare as Exigencies <i>and</i> horribly illegal to boot.<br /> <br /> As for how Exigents relate to the replacement god, it naturally depends on the Exigent and god in question. In an ideal situation (where the Exigent prioritizes his late patron's wishes and the new guy respects his predecessor's works), it should work out nicely. A god thought it was worth sacrificing eternity to empower the mortal, and the Unconquered Sun himself gave his blessing, so the new guy should just be grateful to have an Exalt defending his new purview (situation A). Of course, Creation is rarely ideal. The Exalt could decide to use his powers for his own ends, or the new god might want to govern his domain differently (situation B).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T13:43:30-07:00","id":105061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=104968#post104968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've been curious about is if Exigents are always stronger than their patron god. I guess they are other way what's the main benefit of getting an Exigent? Somebody please enlighten me.</div> </div> </div> </div>No definite statements, but probably not. My expectation is that it has more to do with what the god is willing or able to pay for the flame of Exigence.<br /> <br /> For example, Ahlat might Exalt champions roughly equivalent to the Dragon-Blooded, despite his great personal power, because self-sacrifice isn't in his nature. Meanwhile, the petty harvest god Ten Sheaves surrenders the totality of his being to create a lone Exalted who outstrips him by far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T14:01:00-07:00","id":105072,"title":"","content":"This explains why most gods are jerks, the ones with a sense of altruism probably sacrificed themselves during the Fair Folk invasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T14:29:28-07:00","id":105092,"title":"","content":"How I view this is quite simple, Exigents are Exalts of lesser gods, and if that deity dies, either during or after the exaltation, a replacement will probably follow. However the Exigent has no need to be loyal either to their original or new deity, only to continue acting as an exalt, a super-natural hero of Creation, and in the views of the Celestial Bureaucracy, they are individuals that stand between Celestial Exalts and the Dragon Blooded. And just as Solars beet up and put corrupt little gods in their place. They have no special loyalty to their patron or their patron's replacement, only bargaining and personal choice can make them obey that deity. <br /> <br /> So it really doesn't matter if the Exigent's patron dies or vanishes, they just got a particular set of powers that makes them a hero against what ever that little god though was a threat to Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T14:52:45-07:00","id":105104,"title":"","content":"The Incarna empowered mortals to evade the geas over them to never attack their creators. I wonder if spirits make exigents also to bypass some bureaucratic or celestial issues?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T15:23:29-07:00","id":105132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die#post104955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Exigent's power comes from and is of the nature of his patron. But what happens if that patron can't do his job anymore? Or even worse: Was slain.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;To that end, I recommend that we set up an interdepartmental committee with fairly broad terms of reference so that at the end of the day we'll be in the position to think through the various implications and arrive at a decision based on long-term considerations rather than rush prematurely into precipitate and possibly ill-conceived action which might well have unforeseen repercussions.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T16:00:26-07:00","id":105152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.Jaxus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=105092#post105092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How I view this is quite simple, Exigents are Exalts of lesser gods, and if that deity dies, either during or after the exaltation, a replacement will probably follow. However the Exigent has no need to be loyal either to their original or new deity, only to continue acting as an exalt, a super-natural hero of Creation, and in the views of the Celestial Bureaucracy, they are individuals that stand between Celestial Exalts and the Dragon Blooded. And just as Solars beet up and put corrupt little gods in their place. They have no special loyalty to their patron or their patron's replacement, only bargaining and personal choice can make them obey that deity.<br /> <br /> So it really doesn't matter if the Exigent's patron dies or vanishes, they just got a particular set of powers that makes them a hero against what ever that little god though was a threat to Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they're more like (the) avengers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T16:35:39-07:00","id":105174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=105072#post105072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This explains why most gods are jerks, the ones with a sense of altruism probably sacrificed themselves during the Fair Folk invasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a major reason why Exigents exist specifically as chosen of lesser gods rather than any spirit is to challenge this perception of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T12:42:10-07:00","id":105754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=105152#post105152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they're more like (the) avengers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought of it like that, but yes, they do seem to be the avengers to the Solar's X-men.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T19:00:22-07:00","id":105970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=104968#post104968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've been curious about is if Exigents are always stronger than their patron god. I guess they are other way what's the main benefit of getting an Exigent? Somebody please enlighten me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harvest Maiden Janest is certainly going to be better at reaving down a raksha horde in defense of her village's fields than whatever field-god empowered her was. Champions are a useful thing to have!<br /> <br /> Statements in the form of &quot;Are Exigents always ______&quot; will generally be answered with a no. Exigents don't fit nicely in any box defined by most absolutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T21:57:16-07:00","id":106040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=105970#post105970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harvest Maiden Janest is certainly going to be better at reaving down a raksha horde in defense of her village's fields than whatever field-god empowered her was. Champions are a useful thing to have!<br /> <br /> Statements in the form of &quot;Are Exigents always ______&quot; will generally be answered with a no. Exigents don't fit nicely in any box defined by most absolutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exigents (and all of the other Exalts) really should be greater than their patron god in several, if not most ways, though. It feels right, at the very least, and I would enjoy seeing it. /two cents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T03:21:50-07:00","id":106178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=105970#post105970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harvest Maiden Janest is certainly going to be better at reaving down a raksha horde in defense of her village's fields than whatever field-god empowered her was. Champions are a useful thing to have!<br /> <br /> Statements in the form of &quot;Are Exigents always ______&quot; will generally be answered with a no. Exigents don't fit nicely in any box defined by most absolutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... who was the God of Undergarments again? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T09:26:55-07:00","id":106326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=104968#post104968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've been curious about is if Exigents are always stronger than their patron god. I guess they are other way what's the main benefit of getting an Exigent? Somebody please enlighten me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had some thoughts on the matter.<br /> <br /> Even if the Exigence doesn't increase the power, in 1st and 2nd edition most spirits have more power than they really know what to do with as shown by their enormous essence pools, ability to shift between material/immaterial and reform from any death that doesn't shatter their essence pattern. If Exigence just allowed even a weak god who was sacrificing themselves to get a fair trade in for those powers for ones that are more immediately useful and then give them to someone who is already pretty capable, the results would be understandably scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T09:27:12-07:00","id":106327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=106178#post106178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... who was the God of Undergarments again? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Izarin, the Tailor of Discrete Silks, is not one so inclined towards so overt an agenda as would require an Exigent. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:04:48-07:00","id":106351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=106040#post106040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigents (and all of the other Exalts) really should be greater than their patron god in several, if not most ways, though. It feels right, at the very least, and I would enjoy seeing it. /two cents</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Greater&quot; is subjective.<br /> <br /> The Exigent can do things the god could never do as well... but the god was immortal and wouldn't die even when killed.<br /> <br /> Compared to their patrons, Exalted burn brighter, but also burn <i>out</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:05:21-07:00","id":106352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=106040#post106040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigents (and all of the other Exalts) really should be greater than their patron god in several, if not most ways, though. It feels right, at the very least</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is that?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:05:30-07:00","id":106353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=106327#post106327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Izarin, the Tailor of <b>Discrete Silks</b>, is not one so inclined towards so overt an agenda as would require an Exigent. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Distinct units of silks? You know, I suppose it's one occasion where the other word almost fits. (^VVVVVVVV^)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:14:32-07:00","id":106363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=106352#post106352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is that?</div> </div> </div> </div> You don't need an Exalted champion to solve a problem you can deal with on your own. I suspect Exigents will tend to surpass their patrons in terms of breadth rather than straight power though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:38:57-07:00","id":106378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=106363#post106363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need an Exalted champion to solve a problem you can deal with on your own. I suspect Exigents will tend to surpass their patrons in terms of breadth rather than straight power though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Case in point, Ten Sheaves' breadth didn't really cover kicking ass, which is what he dearly wanted to do to the Fair Folk who would make him wish for death if he didn't go ahead and kill himself.<br /> <br /> If Ten Sheaves was instead facing a crop-plague that would wipe out all of the grains in the area... well, that's the sort of problem that falls very squarely within his powers to solve.<br /> <br /> But if for some reason his Exigent would be able to attain superior powers in that regard in a short enough span of time (because Exalted learn and grow faster than gods), he probably would Exalt someone other than Janest. Someone with more academic knowledge regarding plants and disease, rather than skill at busting heads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:11:50-07:00","id":106397,"title":"","content":"Tiresias hit the pragmatic answer I was going to give, but there is also the thematic of the mixing of divine power and mortal energies producing something greater than the sum of it's parts that is poetically proper to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:03:57-07:00","id":106501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/104955-ascension-for-exigents-where-gods-go-to-die?p=106363#post106363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't need an Exalted champion to solve a problem you can deal with on your own. I suspect Exigents will tend to surpass their patrons in terms of breadth rather than straight power though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe for Exigents.<br /> <br /> I'm really thinking of the &quot;all of the Exalted&quot; side.<br /> <br /> If the gods were incapable of harming the Primordials, geasing them seems to be patently unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Which I prefer, as I prefer the gods to have the capacity to be credible antagonists to the Exalted. Or allies, for that matter.<br /> <br /> The geas should give an indication of a situation in which &quot;problems you can't deal with&quot; have nothing whatsoever to do with how powerful you are.<br /> <br /> Not to mention how there can be gods who have priorities for their Chosen other than &quot;dealing with problems that you can't&quot;, whether it be just a personal or ideological investment in empowering humans, or wanting them to serve as your distant champion or emissary, or handle things you don't want to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}